<title>USA: U.S. intellectual property reforms proposed.</title>
<headline>U.S. intellectual property reforms proposed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new chairman of the House Courts and Intellectual Property subcommittee said Friday he would promote reforms to protect property rights.</p>
<p>&quot;The United States is by far the world's largest producer of intellectual property,&quot; Rep. Howard Coble, R-N.C., said in a statement. &quot;This success is due to the great creativity of our citizens, along with the direct result of a sound and rational policy of protecting intellectual property by encouraging the development of new inventions and processes.&quot;</p>
</text>
